    "b-sks-overview-intro": {
      "id": "b-sks-overview-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The Knowledge System becomes a codebase expert memory: it records what files, functions, fields, variables, and game concepts mean; how strongly each interpretation is supported; and what has already been tried. Beliefs, attempt history, operational events, the raw knowledge sources, and derived graph projections remain separate so each can be searched and maintained according to its own truth model."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-overview-taxonomy": {
      "id": "b-sks-overview-taxonomy",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Raw material lives in five knowledge sources, in two classes. Archival sources — Discord, pull requests, wiki — are raw inputs frozen once ingested: new material appends and gets indexed, existing rows never change. Operational sources — attempts (the target ledger wearing its evidence hat) and code (the active checkout, the only drifting source) — grow with the run itself. Every claim in the graph cites into a source through a typed locator. Standards are part of the knowledge system but outside the knowledge graph: QA-owned authored rules, injected at worker boot and enforced at the ship gate, never citable as evidence."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-overview-decision": {
      "id": "b-sks-overview-decision",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Proposal decision — rebuild projections, selectively migrate knowledge",
        "tone": "success"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Do not edit the existing ledger in place. Preserve it as an immutable audit source, classify every record into the new record families or quarantine, import only evidence-resolvable semantic assertions and useful attempt memory into fresh canonical stores, then destroy and deterministically rebuild the graph and search indexes. A full semantic reset remains the fallback if classification cannot meet the migration gates."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
